WEBVTT

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.520
I can't believe Floch
made it here this early.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:28.260
It's all over for us if the Yeagerist
destroy the flying boat.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:31.330
Why haven't they done it?

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.800
Who knows.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:40.360
They're likely unsure that
we're still alive and trying to stop Eren.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.600
Destroying the ship is simple,

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.130
but after the world is destroyed,

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:48.450
it'd take decades to recreate the technology.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.360
I'm sure they'd want a flying boat
to explore the continents once it's empty.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.460
Perhaps their primary goal
in occupying the harbor

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:01.020
was to get the Azumabito with their
ships and technicians under control.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:07.070
However, if they learn that
we're here as well...

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.500
I'm sure they'll smash that flying boat
into pieces in an instant.

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:17.660
Even if we had the power of the Nine Titans,
stopping them would be difficult.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:24.560
But if we falter here, we would have
no chance to take down the Founder.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:26.440
Let's think of a plan--

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:40.380
Rumbling, Rumbling, it's coming

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:43.290
Rumbling, Rumbling

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:46.260
Beware

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.680
Coming for you

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:00.650
All I ever wanted to do was do right things

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:05.320
I've never wanted to be the king, I swear

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:10.280
All I ever wanted to do was save your life

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:15.410
I've never wanted to grab a knife, I swear

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:23.840
Tearless, fearless, burning, burning

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:27.090
You tell me what have I missed

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:30.680
Still wandering in the deep mist

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:36.720
If I lose it all, slip and fall

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.560
I will never look away

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:45.480
If I lose it all, lose it all, lose it all

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:49.400
If I lose it all outside the wall

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.740
Live to die another day

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:55.120
I don't want anything

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.500
I'm just here to...

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.540
Beware

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:12.030
(Traitor)

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:19.100
We have to kill them all at once.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.400
That's our only way to secure the flying boat.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:29.200
We'll use the power of all our Titans
alongside your weapons to do that.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.300
Okay?

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.050
Hold on a second.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.590
Why?

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.820
If we indiscriminately attack the harbor,
the Azumabito will get caught in the crossfire.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:44.670
She's right!

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:46.760
They might be distant relatives to you,

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:50.310
but to us, they're enemies
who attacked our homeland.

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:52.280
No.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:55.640
It'll be a problem if we let
the Azumabito die, Annie.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.270
Isn't that right?

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.300
Indeed.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:04.660
I should be able to pilot
the flying boat on my own.

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:08.460
But without the Azumabito mechanics,

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:11.340
that thing is just
a plain boat with no wings.

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:17.190
Its wings are currently folded
to make it easier to transport by sea.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:21.850
And of course, just extending the wings
won't be enough to make it fly.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.230
It was originally meant to be
transported to the hangar,

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:28.060
receive maintenance inspection
and perform flight drills

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:30.310
before it's used for operations.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:34.210
About how long would that take?

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:36.900
I don't know.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.380
Ask the Azumabito.

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:44.880
I see.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:48.610
So we need to protect the Azumabito

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:51.930
and secure them enough time
to get the flying boat ready.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:53.730
On top of that,

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:56.430
you're also going to tell
me that you don't want

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.760
to kill any of the Yeagerist
trying to stop us?

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.830
I don't want to kill them.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.770
Some of them are our friends
from the Training Corps, you know?

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:08.610
Then what's the plan?

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.070
Tell me.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:13.910
How exactly are we going to keep
the flying boat and the Azumabito safe

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:16.350
while securing them enough time
to get the ship ready

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.860
all without killing the enemies
charging at us?

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:21.790
Tell me, Armin.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.420
Tell me your plan.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.120
Just like you did when you cornered me.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:33.050
That plan doesn't exist.

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:38.420
Either we settle this in one go,
or we mess up and lose the flying boat.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:42.300
Hold up.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.360
We're here to save people!

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:49.470
And yet, the first thing in our plan
is to kill our fellow islanders?!

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:52.080
Why is this happening?!

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:57.590
You're right.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:02.750
To begin with, none of you have
any obligation to do this with us.

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:06.910
Nor any obligation to make
a hard choice like this.

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:10.870
If you'd been in our place that day,

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.700
you probably wouldn't have
chosen to breach the wall.

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:15.660
Unlike us.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:20.860
As I thought, I'm the same as you.

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:22.540
I see...

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:25.300
So that's what he meant!

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.330
The four of you don't have to fight.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:35.180
Just watch from a safe location
together with Gabi and Falco.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:39.950
If the Yeagerist find you, you'll be forced
to decide whether you want it or not.

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:43.730
But don't get involved.

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:49.840
So you're telling us to just
watch you kill each other?

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:55.150
That said, can this really be solved
just with a Titan rampage?

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.970
I'm not interested in
becoming a spectator.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:05.360
I already killed four Yeagerist
with my own hand, anyway.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:10.180
More importantly, humanity
does not have much time left.

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:15.730
I saw the Titans moving from the shore,
giving off a massive amount of steam.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:21.770
Judging by their speed, they've already
arrived on the continent of Marley.

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:26.950
The closest Marley's cities in the northeast
must have been annihilated by now.

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:31.220
I didn't expect they'd cross
the ocean this fast.

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:35.590
Who knows how many have
been killed already.

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.840
Tell us where Eren Yeager is heading!

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:54.250
I'll keep breaking your arm
until you tell me!

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:01.770
Magath!

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.100
There's nothing to fear.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:07.840
I won't kill you.

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:12.320
Well, that's a relief.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:14.400
I've changed my mind.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:18.830
I don't want to die until
I've seen how all of this ends.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:26.540
If you take me with you,
I might tell you Eren's destination.

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:29.110
We must secure the flying boat first.

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:31.870
We don't have the time to torture her now!

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:51.670
Connie.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:52.920
Armin.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:54.310
Mikasa.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:55.660
Jean.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:59.280
I want to apologize
for my behavior last night.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.590
We were wrong.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:06.200
I spoke so flippantly about justice.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:12.890
Even at this late stage, I cowardly
tried to justify my own actions.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:17.300
All because I was afraid
to reflect on myself

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.850
and see the despicable side
of Marley within me.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:23.010
This isn't your responsibility.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:28.470
It's wrong to place the sins of the past
on your shoulder just because of your race.

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:35.260
Pieck, Annie, Reiner.

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:41.020
There's no reason for you to be burdened
with this world's hatred, either.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.230
But...

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:47.660
We do have the responsibility to remember
this foolish, blood-stained history

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:50.150
and pass it to future generations.

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:55.530
Eren Yeager wants to erase everything.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:57.730
We must not let him.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:01.960
So long we continue to avert our eyes
from our own foolish acts...

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:04.180
This hell will never end.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.330
That's why... I beg you.

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:15.870
Please overlook our foolishness
just for now.

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:26.880
I refuse.

00:10:29.590 --> 00:10:32.820
To just stand by with clean hands.

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:49.040
Just look at that steam.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:53.330
I doubt history has ever changed
in one day as dramatically as today.

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:57.530
And of course, we'll make
no exception for Hizuru.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:01.360
Every last trace of its civilization
will be wiped clean,

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:03.970
and it will be reborn as a new land.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:08.160
Freed from all its troubles.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:13.210
All of you just have
to contribute to this island.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:15.220
And fortunately,

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:19.530
Hizuru's best engineers are here, after all.

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:21.230
Right?

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:25.420
If you don't want to lose
any more of your men,

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.800
you should make sure
they do as they're told.

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:33.750
I hate to interrupt you
when you're in such a good mood.

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:34.780
Eh?

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:38.340
But what is this change
you're so happy about?

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:43.670
If you believe that
the Paradis island is safe now,

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:45.670
then I pity you.

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:50.880
All you're doing is making
your world smaller.

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:55.690
The killing will surely continue,
as it always has.

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:02.250
I appreciate your warning.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:05.260
And yes, I have started
to feel the same way.

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:10.390
What is important now is
to know one's place.

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:15.540
We don't need Hizuru's technology.

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:17.630
Flying boats and navigation.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:21.640
We could simply decide that it's too good
for us and give it all up.

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:23.540
That'd nip this unease in the bud.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:25.240
Do you hear me?

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:29.650
What's important is to know your place.

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:31.730
Understand?

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:35.100
Floch! Where are you?!

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:38.390
Where are the Azumabito?!

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:40.220
Armin?!

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:41.310
Floch!

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:44.170
Where have you been?
What are you on about?

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.660
I was chasing the Cart Titan!

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:48.530
They have the Armored with them!

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:50.400
They escaped by the sea!

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:52.320
We will lose them if we don't chase now!

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:54.510
We need the flying boat immediately!

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:57.480
Hurry up and have
the Azumabito get it running!

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:03.030
What are you talking about?

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:05.090
And what are you standing around for?!

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:06.990
Didn't you have anyone
looking after the Cart?!

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.430
Wasn't it obvious
they'd escape to the south?!

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:13.330
They killed Jean and Onyankopon, you know!

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:15.980
Armin! There's the flying boat!

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:22.290
Floch! Hurry up and get
the Azumabito mechanics out here!

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:34.760
Stop!

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:35.930
Stop right there!

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:37.330
Daz! Samuel!

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:38.670
What are you guys doing?!

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:44.150
Are those bombs?!

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:47.670
Disconnect them right now!

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:50.540
We're using that ship to chase after
the remaining Marleyans escaped by the sea!

00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:53.400
- Hold up!
- Both of you, calm down!

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:57.510
Actually, there is suspicion
that you two are working with Marley

00:13:57.530 --> 00:14:03.960
and trying to stop the Rumbling
using this flying boat.

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:08.940
H-How could we ever
do something like that?!

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:10.100
That's right!

00:14:10.130 --> 00:14:12.930
What'd become of this island
if we stopped Eren?!

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:15.430
Y-Yeah, you're right.

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:18.160
We're finally saved now...

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:22.150
...so there's no way you guys would
put this island back into danger, right?

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:25.130
Of course not!

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:26.450
That's a relief.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:30.960
I wouldn't know what to do
if you two betrayed us.

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:32.930
Anyway, just hurry up.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.410
Disconnect those bombs.

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:43.690
But...

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:46.180
I also got the feeling...

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:52.020
...that you might try to stop Eren from
slaughtering anyone, even if they're enemies.

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:06.490
What's wrong?

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:08.770
We disconnected the detonator.

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:16.340
All left is for Floch to hand over
the Azumabito mechanics.

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:22.480
Once the flying boat is ready, we need to
somehow get everyone on it and leave.

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:25.240
If everything works out...

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:27.660
There won't need to be
any pointless bloodshed.

00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:38.750
Don't you think this is strange?

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:44.480
If they knew our enemies would be
fleeing from the south...

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:47.110
it'd be faster to pursue them by locomotive.

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:51.700
Much faster than going by horseback.

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:58.500
Why would they need to sneak around?

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:01.740
No, I don't have any proof.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:03.370
But...

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:07.950
I really should nip any concerns in the bud.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:23.900
We failed!

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:26.990
What happened, Floch?!

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:31.650
Dammit! Kill her!

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:34.400
I'm not dying without a fight!

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:41.950
Ms. Kiyomi!

00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:48.590
We're under attack!

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:52.980
Mikasa, Armin, and Connie
have betrayed Eldia!

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.540
Kill them!

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:02.050
They'll shoot Thunder Spears
through the windows!

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:06.190
Run to the basement!

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:15.180
It started.

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:19.470
Now it comes to this, we must
exterminate the Yeagerist!

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:20.890
Lady Mikasa!

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:29.710
Azumabito! This way!

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:31.930
We'll repel them in the basement!

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:34.010
Come with us if you want to live!

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:47.440
Hey...

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.000
Daz! Stop it!

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:54.550
- Armin!
- Don't move!

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:00.140
Samuel...

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:07.390
Daz, blow up the flying boat now.

00:18:07.970 --> 00:18:09.360
Do it now!

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:14.570
Samuel...

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:16.800
- Hey--
- You betrayed us, right?

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:18.080
Connie.

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:21.110
Didn't we make the promise?

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:23.220
That we'd get more land...

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:26.270
...so we can eat meat together!

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:31.750
Ugh, shit!

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:34.380
Why... must this happen?

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:44.550
At this rate, we'd be
trapped here to death!

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:46.540
It's only a matter of time
before they kill us!

00:18:46.570 --> 00:18:47.880
This is fine.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:52.630
As long as we're safe, they can run wild.

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:55.240
They ran to the basement!

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.130
Bring more explosives!

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:09.490
They want to hole themselves up
in the basement with no escape?

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:19.330
Wait...

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:21.100
Could it be...?!

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:35.580
So it didn't work...

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:39.470
Why does this always happen?

00:19:41.040 --> 00:19:44.290
You can't separate humanity from violence.

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:47.010
Isn't that right, Captain?

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:23.720
Get more Thunder Spears!

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:44.070
Daz! Blow it up!

00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:55.040
Armin!

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:58.580
Stop it!

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:05.950
Please stop it!

00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:07.660
Armin!

00:21:07.690 --> 00:21:09.220
You traitors!

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:11.010
Why?!

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:14.380
Aren't we friends?!

00:21:15.030 --> 00:21:17.170
You guys are our friends!

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:19.890
But...

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:22.370
I...

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:36.020
Someone has to do this!

00:21:51.780 --> 00:21:52.620
S-Stop it--

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:59.200
Someone has to get blood on their hands!

00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:13.150
The iron bullet is the proof of justice

00:22:13.150 --> 00:22:15.730
If it pierces through,
I'll be closer to being a hero

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:18.450
But when I close my eyes and touch

00:22:18.450 --> 00:22:22.990
I notice that the devil
was no different from me

00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:26.450
Why am I not good, but he's okay?

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:29.160
The only thing that
separates us was the wall

00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:31.830
Don't lament on the fate that we're born

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:35.710
Because we're all free

00:22:35.710 --> 00:22:40.970
If only I have wings like birds

00:22:40.970 --> 00:22:46.310
I can go anywhere I want

00:22:46.310 --> 00:22:50.390
But if I don't have a place to return to

00:22:50.390 --> 00:22:55.820
I'm sure I can't go anywhere

00:22:55.820 --> 00:23:00.780
I don't want to just live

00:23:01.160 --> 00:23:11.830
The world is cruel, but I still love you

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:21.930
I will sacrifice anything to protect you

00:23:21.930 --> 00:23:27.140
Even if it's a mistake to do so,
I'll not doubt my actions

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:33.560
Because the right thing
is to firmly believe in yourself

00:23:41.350 --> 00:23:43.080
You die if you hesitate.

00:23:43.460 --> 00:23:46.160
Point the gun and pull the trigger.

00:23:46.670 --> 00:23:51.590
Believing that there's a path forward
beyond this betrayal.

00:23:52.280 --> 00:23:54.890
Next time, \"Retrospective.\"
